    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dbcddad3-dd5f-56f5-b5ec-d9b5a793006c",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 \\\\ -5 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
