      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -6 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
